angement behind an extra lookup.",correction:"Show the name, price and renewal terms before requesting a choice.",counts:"Counts lookups and choices. Selecting a renewing plan records a task error, not a personal failing."},{name:"Accessibility",description:"Information and operation available across abilities and technologies.",learn:"Identify why color needs equivalent information.",instructions:"Observe the sample and say what you can conclude. If it only shows color without a legend, you can say it is not possible to tell.",good:"Text and a symbol communicate that the connection was interrupted.",bad:"An isolated color does not express an unambiguous status.",correction:"Add text, a symbol and an accessible announcement when status changes.",counts:"Counts the answer. A status unsupported by the available information records an error. This is not a WCAG audit."},{name:"Awareness",description:"Understanding the state, changes and next step of an operation.",learn:"Distinguish a finished operation from understandable confirmation.",instructions:"Write a note and save it in this activity. After the simulated delay, say whether the sample confirms saving.",good:"The sample reports saving, then confirms the outcome.",bad:"The operation finishes without communicating whether the note was saved.",correction:"Communicate progress, outcome and next step without relying on memory.",counts:"Counts saving and answering. An answer unsupported by the sample records an error. The delay is simulated, not server performance."},{name:"Ethical engagement",description:"Voluntary participation with clear value, without pressure or barriers to leaving.",learn:"Separate a free decision from a pressuring invitation.",instructions:"Read the invitation and choose to continue with or without notifications. Both decisions are valid.",good:"The option is explained and an equivalent way out is offered.",bad:"The sample uses pressure about a fictional streak to promote notifications.",correct